subprocess --  Run Shell Commands from Python  // subprocess is the most powerful DevOps library — it can run ANY command you type in terminal, from inside Python! 🚀
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
🔄 os vs subprocess — Same Task Different Way

Task             | os way                         | subprocess way
-----------------|--------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------
Create folder    | os.makedirs('/tmp/test')      | subprocess.run(['mkdir', '-p', '/tmp/test'])

Delete file      | os.remove('file.txt')         | subprocess.run(['rm', 'file.txt'])

List files       | os.listdir('/home')           | subprocess.run(['ls', '/home'])

Check disk       | ❌ can't do                    | subprocess.run(['df', '-h'])

Restart service  | ❌ can't do                    | subprocess.run(['systemctl', 'restart', 'nginx'])

Run git          | ❌ can't do                    | subprocess.run(['git', 'pull'])


📊 Summary Table

Category        Tasks
---------------------------------------------------------
Basic           run, check, shell commands

Output          capture stdout, stderr, returncode

Files           mkdir, rm, cp, mv, find

System          df, free, ps, kill, uptime

Services        start, stop, restart, status

